Scott's Example 1.2 is the neighbourhood system on the tokens {0, 1} whose neighbourhoods are the master, {0}, and {1}, with the master as largest neighbourhood. The master is nonempty and is a neighbourhood, every set of tokens is contained in it, and a neighbourhood contained in an intersection of two neighbourhoods is again a neighbourhood, because that intersection is the master, {0}, {1}, or empty, and the empty case admits no neighbourhood.
